From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:48:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tests: test the frame-sequential stereo mode flag

Test the frame of DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_SEQUENTIAL with two CTA-861
formats, 1080p60 (VIC 16) and 720p120 (VIC 47): the link keeps the 2D
timing and clock through drm_mode_set_crtcinfo() and
drm_mode_stereo_clock(), drm_mode_get_hv_timing() gives twice the width
for the side by side buffer, and drm_mode_validate_driver() accepts the
layout while still refusing the next value.

Test the connector opt-in on a pipeline of a DisplayPort connector whose
modes are VIC 16 in 2D, in frame packing and in frame sequential, for the
four combinations of stereo_allowed and stereo_frame_sequential_allowed:
the probe helper keeps frame packing only with stereo_allowed and frame
sequential only with stereo_frame_sequential_allowed, and an atomic
commit of the frame-sequential mode fails with -EINVAL unless the
connector opted in, while the 2D mode always commits.

Assisted-by: LLM
